--TEST--
A string literal at a parameter whose union holds a class and one `string<K>`, `property<T>` or `propertyPath<T>` member reports that member's error for a wrong name, and a union with two such members keeps the literal a `string` — `rule:types/property-key`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A wrong name in a literal at such a union is reported at the name.
final class Filter
{
}

class Order
{
    public string $name = "o1";
    public int $total = 40;

    public static function find(string<propertyPath<static>>|Filter $condition): uint
    {
        return 0;
    }

    public static function column(?property<Order>|Filter $field): uint
    {
        return 0;
    }

    public static function either(property<Order>|propertyPath<Order> $field): uint
    {
        return 0;
    }
}

// `missing` is not a property of `Order`.
uint $a = Order::find("{missing} = ?");
// `totl` is misspelled.
uint $b = Order::column("totl");
// Two checked string types: the literal stays a `string`.
uint $c = Order::either("name");
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Order` has no public property `$missing`
   --> %s:29:25
   |
29 | uint $a = Order::find("{missing} = ?");
   |                         ^^^^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: each part of a property path names a public property of the class the path has reached: `Order` has `$name`, `$total`

error[E0405]: `Order` has no public property `$totl`
   --> %s:31:25
   |
31 | uint $b = Order::column("totl");
   |                         ^^^^^^ this name is checked here
   = help: a property name written in the code is checked when the program compiles. The public properties of `Order` are: `$name`, `$total`

error[E0401]: expected `propertyPath<Order>|property<Order>`, found `string`
   --> %s:33:25
   |
33 | uint $c = Order::either("name");
   |                         ^^^^^^ this is `string`

error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
